MID_SE_Urs_Bon_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Urs_Bon_C_001: Ah, hello, Bonaventure. Is there something you need?
MID_SE_Urs_Bon_C_002: Ah, Ursula. One of our warriors told me you did\nhim a good turn.
MID_SE_Urs_Bon_C_003: I believe he said you saved him from "losing the\nshirt off his back" to a cunning merchant.
MID_SE_Urs_Bon_C_004: Ah... Something of an exaggeration, I fear.
MID_SE_Urs_Bon_C_005: I simply pointed out that the numbers were inflated\nand requested that the transaction be a fair one.
MID_SE_Urs_Bon_C_006: They were using complex calculations to confuse\nthe process, and I provided exact figures in response.
MID_SE_Urs_Bon_C_007: You defused a delicate situation with an appropriate\nresponse. Your gift for numbers served us well.
MID_SE_Urs_Bon_C_008: Once again, you have my gratitude for intervening.
MID_SE_Urs_Bon_C_009: It was nothing. Anyone else would do the same.
MID_SE_Urs_Bon_C_010: We value the people of Saramis as customers.\nIt's important to us that they are treated well.
MID_SE_Urs_Bon_C_011: Intelligent, beautiful, and humble too? You are a\nrare sort of maiden.
MID_SE_Urs_Bon_C_012: I'm honored, but I think you're overstating it.
MID_SE_Urs_Bon_C_013: Besides, I'm nearly 80 years old. Hardly young\nenough to still be a maiden.
MID_SE_Urs_Bon_C_014: Pardon?! You are older than me? Why, I would guess\nyou to be half my age.
MID_SE_Urs_Bon_C_015: Yes, people are often surprised when I tell them.\nIt's a nice icebreaker during business meetings.
MID_SE_Urs_Bon_C_016: Now, if you'll excuse me, I still have some work\nleft to do.
MID_SE_Urs_Bon_C_017: O-of course. My apologies for taking up your time.
MID_SE_Urs_Bon_C_018: Not at all. As always, we here at Vandahl Trading\nappreciate your patronage.
MID_SE_Urs_Bon_C_019: No wonder she is so skilled, with decades of\nexperience behind her.
MID_SE_Urs_Bon_C_020: What a rare talent. If only we could recruit her\nto the Saraminian court!
MID_SE_Urs_Bon_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Urs_Bon_B_001: Ursula, is there nothing I can say to convince you to\nleave your employer and serve Saramis?
MID_SE_Urs_Bon_B_002: Hello to you too. Now, where is this coming from?
MID_SE_Urs_Bon_B_003: I have a high opinion of your character—and your\ntalents. I would see them put to use for us.
MID_SE_Urs_Bon_B_004: Her Majesty Queen Theodora is the sort of strong\nruler worth devoting one's life to.
MID_SE_Urs_Bon_B_005: Would it not be an honor for you to enter into\nher service?
MID_SE_Urs_Bon_B_006: You will not be paid in honor, mind you. We know\nyour worth and would pay you accordingly.
MID_SE_Urs_Bon_B_007: I appreciate your offer, but I must decline.
MID_SE_Urs_Bon_B_008: So you will not consider it? There must be some\nreason for that.
MID_SE_Urs_Bon_B_009: My loyalty is to Talimun. To me, he is more precious\nthan any other prize.
MID_SE_Urs_Bon_B_010: No matter the terms offered, I will never leave\nthe Vandahl Trading Company.
MID_SE_Urs_Bon_B_011: Intelligence, dignity, and loyalty as well?! Your\nrefusal pains me all the more!
MID_SE_Urs_Bon_B_012: But I can see you are as devoted to Talimun as I am\nto Her Majesty.
MID_SE_Urs_Bon_B_013: Just as I would never turn my back on Saramis,\nI gather you would remain true to your company.
MID_SE_Urs_Bon_B_014: Exactly. So you must understand why I will\nnever leave.
MID_SE_Urs_Bon_B_015: Though it breaks my heart, I do. I withdraw the\nproposal out of respect for your loyalty.
MID_SE_Urs_Bon_B_016: However, I do see this as a rare chance to extend\nan offer for tea.
MID_SE_Urs_Bon_B_017: I find myself increasingly interested in you. I should\nlike to hear more of your life.
MID_SE_Urs_Bon_B_018: It would be my pleasure. I'm interested in hearing\nyour insights as Saramis's Living Archive.
MID_SE_Urs_Bon_B_019: And coincidentally, we've just acquired an item\nthat would be perfect for you.
MID_SE_Urs_Bon_B_020: Interesting. What is it?
MID_SE_Urs_Bon_B_021: It's an unusual vessel fashioned with a mustache\nguard—perfect for our upcoming teatime.
MID_SE_Urs_Bon_B_022: If you'd like, I could secure you one now at\na substantial discount. Interested?
MID_SE_Urs_Bon_B_023: Ohoho! You do not miss an opportunity, I see.\nAh, what might have been!